{
  "title": "68: al-Qalam القلم",
  "code": "02",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nنٓ وَالْقَلَمِ وَمَا يَسْطُرُونَ (1)\nNun’ and (N) by the Pen and by what they write\nمَآ اَنتَ بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ بِمَجْنُونٍ (2)\nThou (O’ Our Prophet!) by the grace of thy Lord, art not mad\nوَاِنَّ لَكَ لَاَجْرًا غَيْرَ مَمْنُونٍ (3)\nAnd verily there is for thee a recompense unending (unobliging)\nوَاِنَّكَ لَعَلَىٰ خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ (4)\nAnd most certainly thou standest on sublime morality\nفَسَتُبْصِرُ وَيُبْصِرُونَ (5)\nSo thou wilt see and they (too) wilt see\nبِاَييِّكُمُ الْمَفْتُونُ (6)\nWhich of you is demented\nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَن ضَلَّ عَن سَبِيلِهِۦ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُهْتَدِينَ (7)\nVerily thy Lord! He knoweth best of him who is astray from His way, and He knoweth best of those guided aright\nفَلَا تُطِعِ الْمُكَذِّبِينَ (8)\nSo yield thou not to the beliers!\nوَدُّوا۟ لَوْ تُدْهِنُ فَيُدْهِنُونَ (9)\nWish they that thou shouldst be pliant so they (too) would be pliant\nوَلَا تُطِعْ كُلَّ حَلَّافٍ مَّهِينٍ (10)\nAnd yield thou not unto any despicable swearer\nهَمَّازٍ مَّشَّآءٍۭ بِنَمِيمٍ (11)\nDefamer, going about with slander\nمَّنَّاعٍ لِّلْخَيْرِ مُعْتَدٍ اَثِيمٍ (12)\nVehement hinderer of good, uncontrolled transgressor, sunk deep in sin\nعُتُلٍّۭ بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ زَنِيمٍ (13)\nCruelly violent, besides all that, baseborn\nاَن كَانَ ذَا مَالٍ وَبَنِينَ (14)\nJust because possesses he wealth and sons\nاِذَا تُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْهِ ءَايٰتُنَا قَالَ اَسٰطِيرُ الْاَوَّلِينَ (15)\nWhen unto him are recited Our signs, sayeth he: (they are the) “Stories of yore” (legends of the ancients)\nسَنَسِمُهُۥ عَلَى الْخُرْطُومِ (16)\nWe will brand him on the snout!\nاِنَّا بَلَوْنٰهُمْ كَمَا بَلَوْنَآ اَصْحٰبَ الْجَنَّةِ اِذْ اَقْسَمُوا۟ لَيَصْرِمُنَّهَا مُصْبِحِينَ (17)\nVerily We will try them as We did try the owners of the garden, when they vowed that they would certainly pluck the fruits at morn\nوَلَا يَسْتَثْنُونَ (18)\nAnd made no (room for) exception (for the will of God) (saying ‘If God willeth it’)\nفَطَافَ عَلَيْهَا طَآئِفٌ مِّن رَّبِّكَ وَهُمْ نَآئِمُونَ (19)\nSo encircled it a visitation from thy Lord, (rendering the garden desolate) while they were asleep\nفَاَصْبَحَتْ كَالصَّرِيمِ (20)\nAnd it became like black barren soil\nفَتَنَادَوْا۟ مُصْبِحِينَ (21)\nAnd they cried out one unto each other at morn\nاَنِ اغْدُوا۟ عَلَىٰ حَرْثِكُمْ اِن كُنتُمْ صٰرِمِينَ (22)\nBe ye early at your tilth if ye would pluck (the fruits)\nفَانطَلَقُوا۟ وَهُمْ يَتَخٰفَتُونَ (23)\nAnd went they whispering unto each other\nاَن لَّا يَدْخُلَنَّهَا الْيَوْمَ عَلَيْكُم مِّسْكِينٌ (24)\nSaying: “No poor man shall enter it today upon you\nوَغَدَوْا۟ عَلَىٰ حَرْدٍ قٰدِرِينَ (25)\nAnd at morn went they, strong in their resolve (to prevent the poor)\nفَلَمَّا رَاَوْهَا قَالُوٓا۟ اِنَّا لَضَآلُّونَ (26)\nBut when they beheld it, said they: “Verily we have strayed!\nبَلْ نَحْنُ مَحْرُومُونَ (27)\nNay! we are (the) deprived ones (of the fruits of our labour).\nقَالَ اَوْسَطُهُمْ اَلَمْ اَقُل لَّكُمْ لَوْلَا تُسَبِّحُونَ (28)\nSaid the most balanced one of them: “Said I not unto you, ‘Why should ye not glorify (God)’?\nقَالُوا۟ سُبْحٰنَ رَبِّنَآ اِنَّا كُنَّا ظٰلِمِينَ (29)\nSaid they: “Hallowed be Our Lord! Verily we have been unjust!\nفَاَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ يَتَلٰوَمُونَ (30)\nThen some of them proceeded against the others, reproaching each other\nقَالُوا۟ يٰوَيْلَنَآ اِنَّا كُنَّا طٰغِينَ (31)\nSaid they: “O’ woe unto us! Verily we have been arrogant!\nعَسَىٰ رَبُّنَآ اَن يُبْدِلَنَا خَيْرًا مِّنْهَآ اِنَّآ اِلَىٰ رَبِّنَا رٰغِبُونَ (32)\nHapply, our Lord will give us in exchange a better one than it; Verily unto our Lord do we turn (in repentance)\nكَذٰلِكَ الْعَذَابُ وَلَعَذَابُ الْءَاخِرَةِ اَكْبَرُ لَوْ كَانُوا۟ يَعْلَمُونَ (33)\nSuch hath been Our chastisement, and certainly the chastisement of the hereafter is greater still; Did they but know (it)!\nاِنَّ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ عِندَ رَبِّهِمْ جَنّٰتِ النَّعِيمِ (34)\nVerily, for the pious ones with their Lord are the Gardens of bliss\nاَفَنَجْعَلُ الْمُسْلِمِينَ كَالْمُجْرِمِينَ (35)\nWhat! shall We then make the ‘Muslims’ like unto the guilty ones?\nمَا لَكُمْ كَيْفَ تَحْكُمُونَ (36)\nWhat is the matter with you? How judge ye\nاَمْ لَكُمْ كِتٰبٌ فِيهِ تَدْرُسُونَ (37)\nOr have ye a scripture wherein ye read?\nاِنَّ لَكُمْ فِيهِ لَمَا تَخَيَّرُونَ (38)\nVerily, therein is for you what ye choose?\nاَمْ لَكُمْ اَيْمٰنٌ عَلَيْنَا بٰلِغَةٌ اِلَىٰ يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ اِنَّ لَكُمْ لَمَا تَحْكُمُونَ (39)\nOr have ye a sworn covenant from Us tending to the Day of Judgment that ye shall surely have whatever ye judge?\nسَلْهُمْ اَيُّهُم بِذٰلِكَ زَعِيمٌ (40)\nAsk them (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) which of them will guarantee that!\nاَمْ لَهُمْ شُرَكَآءُ فَلْيَاْتُوا۟ بِشُرَكَآئِهِمْ اِن كَانُوا۟ صٰدِقِينَ (41)\nOr have they any ‘Partners’ (to Us)? Then let them bring their partners (associate gods) if they be truthful!\nيَوْمَ يُكْشَفُ عَن سَاقٍ وَيُدْعَوْنَ اِلَى السُّجُودِ فَلَا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ (42)\nOn the Day that the shin shall be laid bare, (i.e. befalleth an affliction), and they shall be called upon to prostrate in obeisance, but they shall not be able (to do it)\nخٰشِعَةً اَبْصٰرُهُمْ تَرْهَقُهُمْ ذِلَّةٌ وَقَدْ كَانُوا۟ يُدْعَوْنَ اِلَى السُّجُودِ وَهُمْ سٰلِمُونَ (43)\nCasting down their looks, shall cover them abasement, and indeed they had been called upon to prostrate in obeisance, while yet they were whole (healthy)\nفَذَرْنِى وَمَن يُكَذِّبُ بِهٰذَا الْحَدِيثِ سَنَسْتَدْرِجُهُم مِّنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ (44)\nSo leave Me and him who belieth this announcement, We will lead them on (to ruin) by steps from whence they know not\nوَاُمْلِى لَهُمْ اِنَّ كَيْدِى مَتِينٌ (45)\nAnd yet respite them; for verily My device is firm\nاَمْ تَسَْٔلُهُمْ اَجْرًا فَهُم مِّن مَّغْرَمٍ مُّثْقَلُونَ (46)\nOr askest thou from them a recompense that they are burdened with a load of debt?\nاَمْ عِندَهُمُ الْغَيْبُ فَهُمْ يَكْتُبُونَ (47)\nOr with them is the knowledge of the unseen, that they write (it) down?\nفَاصْبِرْ لِحُكْمِ رَبِّكَ وَلَا تَكُن كَصَاحِبِ الْحُوتِ اِذْ نَادَىٰ وَهُوَ مَكْظُومٌ (48)\nSo wait thou patiently for the judgment of thy Lord! Be not thou like unto the Companion of the fish! when cried he when he was confined\nلَّوْلَآ اَن تَدٰرَكَهُۥ نِعْمَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦ لَنُبِذَ بِالْعَرَآءِ وَهُوَ مَذْمُومٌ (49)\nHad not a bounty from his Lord reached him, he would certainly have been cast forth on the naked shore while in disgrace\nفَاجْتَبٰهُ رَبُّهُۥ فَجَعَلَهُۥ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِينَ (50)\nThen chose him his Lord and made him of the righteous ones\nوَاِن يَكَادُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ لَيُزْلِقُونَكَ بِاَبْصٰرِهِمْ لَمَّا سَمِعُوا۟ الذِّكْرَ وَيَقُولُونَ اِنَّهُۥ لَمَجْنُونٌ (51)\nAnd those who disbelieve would almost smite thee with their eyes when they hear the Reminder, and say they: “Verily he is mad\nوَمَا هُوَ اِلَّا ذِكْرٌ لِّلْعٰلَمِينَ (52)\nAnd it is naught but a Reminder unto the worlds (the whole Mankind)",
  "merits": "There are 52 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the one who recites this Surah will never face financial difficulties. Writing this Surah and tying it to any part of the body that is suffering from pain alleviates the pain."
